st do other things with it  and it provides a very convenient uh  sort of mapping system  going back and forth between r objects  and python objects  the way i like to say it is r and python  don't  need to be competitors with one another  the advantages of each of them can  complement one another  very nicely and reticulate will allow  you to do that  so there you have it that's 20 distinct  packages in  r each of them kind of serving a  different purpose  even though you can bundle a bunch of  them together into different categories  of tasks  that you're most likely to do in your  lifetime as a data scientist  and now i say this all the time in my  videos on r  packages but i'm just gonna say it again  here  if you get comfortable with all these  packages let alone master them  you really are going to become a really  strong data scientist  you're really going to go from somebody  that if you started as a beginner or  somebody with no experience  you can consider yourself intermediate  or once you even start mastering these  and the ins and outs of them  maybe even you can start treading into  the advanced territory  so thanks for watching this video if you  enjoyed it please consider  sharing it smash the like button if you  disliked it  hey you can dislike this video too you  can even dislike this video twice  really tell youtube you disliked the  video either way leave me a comment down  below  tell me what your favorite r packages  then i'll see you all in the not so  distant future  until then richard on data
 

